From fc0322aefa4d1ff602a1c5519761d5f3bdfe58a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AaradhyaB18 <bapna.aaradhya2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:03:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix quarter-unit courses (e.g. CS 136L) consuming a full term
 slot

CS 136L is a 0.25-unit companion course but was being treated as a
full course slot in both the planner's greedy scheduler and the
frontend unit tracking, undercounting term load by 0.25 units and
under-filling terms by one elective.

- services/planner.py: 5-course/term cap now only counts courses at
  or above the standard 0.5-unit weight (counts_toward_cap); quarter-
  unit courses are always scheduled alongside without using a slot.
- index.html: mirrors the same UNIT_OVERRIDES/getUnits logic for the
  progress bar, per-course unit labels, and a new per-term unit
  total shown in the grid header.
- tests/test_planner.py: regression coverage for the CS 136L case.

Applies to every program whose typical-term map includes CS 136L,
not just one plan.
---
 index.html            | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 services/planner.py   | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 tests/test_planner.py | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 85 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

